  "notes": [
    "Maximums and minimums are per every 1,000 points unless otherwise stated (p. 167). The builder applies them as written, which is right for armies up to 1,000 points; scale them up yourself for larger armies.",
    "Can recreate formations that crossed into Russia, Lithuanian forces raised on liberation, and the 'Bug Division'.",
    "1 to 2 Infantry Brigades: 1 or 2 Regiments of Polish Infantry (1-4 battalions), plus 0 to 2 Chasseur/Jäger battalions (Lithuanians and Bug Division).",
    "Regimental Artillery: 1 section per 3 battalions and/or 1 battery per infantry regiment of 3+ battalions (section and battery may be mixed).",
    "0 to 1 Cavalry Brigade (1 per 2 Infantry Brigades): 1 or 2 regiments per brigade from up to 1 Hussar, up to 6 Uhlan, up to 3 Chasseur-à-Cheval (army-wide caps).",
    "Divisional Artillery: 0 to 2 Foot Artillery batteries (1 per 7 infantry battalions).",
    "Reserve Artillery: up to 1 Horse battery and up to 1 Heavy Foot battery (each if 8+ infantry battalions taken), attached to any brigade."
  ],
  "alliesRules": [
